import BitcoinProofs.Bip.B10.Bip144

/-!
# BitcoinProofs.Bip.B10.Bip144Vectors — BIP144 consensus kill-vectors

Byte vectors V1–V8 and their verified decode/encode/reject theorems.
Generated by and cross-checked with a python3 reference
against BIP144 (public domain) and Bitcoin Core @ cce32b168
`primitives/transaction.h UnserializeTransaction:212-239`.

Proof note: the four decode theorems are staged — a single kernel
`rfl` over the whole `decodeTx144` evaluation peaks above the suite
watchdog's 15 GB RSS kill-line (measured 20–42 GB), so each parse step
is pinned by a cheap `have … := by rfl` at literal offsets and the
bind chain is discharged by `simp only` + a final literal `rfl`. Every
ingredient was measured ≤ 8.4 GB / ≤ 46 s standalone.
-/

